Hello all,<br>I have an old tyt md-uv380 an looking to play with openGD77. Question on firmware flash and recovery to original.<br><br>I followed directions here to the letter: <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=2380" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=19&amp;t=2380</a><br><br>However I failed to find the extended notes here in time:<br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#backup-before-you-do-anything-else" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... thing-else</a><br><br>So in essence I did the suggested firmware backup but did not do the eeprom, mcu, or calibration backup before my first opendg77 codeplug upload.<br><br>So the questions here are:<br>- did I screw up my ability to revert back to the original firmware<br>- is it possible to get eeprom, mcu, and calibration from another unit and use those?<br><br>In the end it doesn't upset me not being able to revert ... but reverting the firmware might help in some troubleshooting I am doing.<br><br>Thanks<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7956">NV2M</a> — Wed Mar 26, 2025 3:03 pm</p><hr />
